0..59 Comment "// A reflexivity at a point composes with `then` in a type."
60..62 Comment "//"
63..139 Comment "// `here(x)` reads its type off its point\'s binder, whatever type the binder"
140..217 Comment "// writes: `Path(A, x, x)` when `x : A`. A composite whose first operand is a"
218..283 Comment "// reflexivity, or ends in one, takes its type from that reading."
284..286 Comment "//"
287..347 Comment "// Each declaration states such a composite in its own type."
348..350 Comment "//"
351..416 Comment "// - see: #3834 — a reflexivity first in `then`, refused before"
418..493 Comment "/// A reflexivity stands first in the type\'s composite. The left unit holds"
494..570 Comment "/// up to a path, not by computation, so the composite stands on both sides."
